  "label": "User projected onto Michelle Obama's skeptical expression and the textual claim of 'zero' pregnancy photos",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Michelle Obama's skeptical facial expression and the textual material stating 'zero' pictures of her pregnancy. The user is implicitly identifying with the meme's stance — either mocking the claim or adopting the dismissive attitude — by projecting themselves onto the visual and textual elements that convey denial and judgment. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the meme (visual expression + text) creates an implicit identification with the meme's perspective, making the user feel they are the one making the claim or judging the situation.",
